                                        {
                                            "no": 19,
                                            "type": "INVOICE",
                                            "note": "Minimum age to drive is 20 (with some exceptions – see below) but between 20 - 24 years inclusive a young driver fee applies of $19 plus taxes and fees per day payable on arrival (unless you have purchased the Go Premier package which includes the underage driver fee for 1 young driver). If you rent an electric vehicle no package includes the young driver fee so this is always payable locally on arrival. \n\nHowever, the minimum age is 25 to drive the following vehicles: \n\nInfiniti QX50 or similar INTERMEDIATE ELITE SUV 2WD/4WD \nInfiniti Q50 or similar STANDARD ELITE 2/4 DR \nInfiniti QX80 or similar LUXURY LARGE SUV \nChevy/Ford CAMARO/MUSTANG \n\nIn the states of Alabama and Nebraska, the minimum rental age is 19. For renters age 19, the young renter fee is $52.00 per day. For Young Renters ages 20 – 24, the renter is $19.00 per day\nIn the states of New York and Michigan, the minimum rental age is 18. The Young Renter fee is $52.00 per day for renters ages 18 and 19. Renters ages 18 and 19 in New York and Michigan may rent car classes A – F only.\nIn Michigan, renters between ages 18 and 24 may be signed on as an Additional driver on Michigan rentals only. The appropriate Young driver fee will be added, in addition to the AAO charge. If both the renter and AAO are under 25, only one Young Driver fee will be assessed.\nOnly one young driver (ages 20-24) can be added as a primary driver, or as an additional driver per rental contract.\n-\tIn New York, a renter must be 20 years and older to be added as an additional driver; but young renters ages 18 – 19 can rent as a primary driver only.\n-\tIn Michigan, where the minimum rental age is 18, young renters ages 18 – 24 may be signed on as an additional driver on Michigan rentals only.\n-\tIn Alabama and Nebraska, where the minimum rental age is 19, only one young driver can be added as a primary driver, or as an additional driver per rental contract.\nIf you have purchased the Hertz Go Premier package the Young driver fee is included",
                                            "systemGenerated": true,
                                            "noteId": 0
                                        },
                                        {
                                            "no": 20,
                                            "type": "ITINERARY",
                                            "note": "Minimum age to drive is 20 (with some exceptions – see below) but between 20 - 24 years inclusive a young driver fee applies of $19 plus taxes and fees per day payable on arrival (unless you have purchased the Go Premier package which includes the underage driver fee for 1 young driver). If you rent an electric vehicle no package includes the young driver fee so this is always payable locally on arrival. \n\nHowever, the minimum age is 25 to drive the following vehicles: \n\nInfiniti QX50 or similar INTERMEDIATE ELITE SUV 2WD/4WD \nInfiniti Q50 or similar STANDARD ELITE 2/4 DR \nInfiniti QX80 or similar LUXURY LARGE SUV \nChevy/Ford CAMARO/MUSTANG \n\nIn the states of Alabama and Nebraska, the minimum rental age is 19. For renters age 19, the young renter fee is $52.00 per day. For Young Renters ages 20 – 24, the renter is $19.00 per day\nIn the states of New York and Michigan, the minimum rental age is 18. The Young Renter fee is $52.00 per day for renters ages 18 and 19. Renters ages 18 and 19 in New York and Michigan may rent car classes A – F only.\nIn Michigan, renters between ages 18 and 24 may be signed on as an Additional driver on Michigan rentals only. The appropriate Young driver fee will be added, in addition to the AAO charge. If both the renter and AAO are under 25, only one Young Driver fee will be assessed.\nOnly one young driver (ages 20-24) can be added as a primary driver, or as an additional driver per rental contract.\n-\tIn New York, a renter must be 20 years and older to be added as an additional driver; but young renters ages 18 – 19 can rent as a primary driver only.\n-\tIn Michigan, where the minimum rental age is 18, young renters ages 18 – 24 may be signed on as an additional driver on Michigan rentals only.\n-\tIn Alabama and Nebraska, where the minimum rental age is 19, only one young driver can be added as a primary driver, or as an additional driver per rental contract.\nIf you have